WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.631
For three years, Ethan Drake had carried the heaviest burdens

2
00:00:02.631 --> 00:00:05.262
of the Vanguard Guild.

3
00:00:05.262 --> 00:00:08.957
While the elite strike teams claimed the glory, the press

4
00:00:08.957 --> 00:00:12.652
conferences, and the multi-million credit bounties, Ethan walked three paces

5
00:00:12.652 --> 00:00:16.347
behind—an unranked core porter whose mana channels had been deemed

6
00:00:16.347 --> 00:00:20.042
permanently fractured since birth.

7
00:00:20.042 --> 00:00:22.735
He was the invisible mule of Sector Nine...

8
00:00:22.735 --> 00:00:23.935
until tonight.

9
00:00:23.935 --> 00:00:27.505
Across the grand banquet hall of House Vance, beneath crystal

10
00:00:27.505 --> 00:00:31.075
chandeliers that mirrored the cold rain beating against the high

11
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:34.645
windows, his loyalty was publicly auctioned.

12
00:00:34.645 --> 00:00:37.276
Lady Evelyn Cross did not lower her voice.

13
00:00:37.276 --> 00:00:38.967
She did not avert her gaze.

14
00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:42.725
With a single, dismissive flick of her manicured fingers, she

15
00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:46.483
cast their silver engagement band across the marble floor.

16
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:49.364
The ring bounced against the stone, coming to a dead

17
00:00:49.364 --> 00:00:52.245
stop against Ethan's worn combat boots.

18
00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:55.669
Standing beside her was Captain Marcus Vance—an A-Rank vanguard clad

19
00:00:55.669 --> 00:00:59.093
in bespoke titanium alloy, a predator who commanded the city’s

20
00:00:59.093 --> 00:01:02.517
most lucrative dungeon licences.

21
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:06.432
Evelyn stepped seamlessly into Marcus’s shadow, trading three years of

22
00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:10.347
shared survival for the security of a noble bloodline.

23
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.260
Marcus did not draw his blade.

24
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.980
In the upper circles of the Awakened nobility, physical violence

25
00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.700
was uncouth when social annihilation was so effortless.

26
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.815
With a single gesture to the guild bailiffs, Marcus revoked

27
00:01:23.815 --> 00:01:26.930
Ethan’s porter licence on grounds of physical deficiency, stripping him

28
00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:30.045
of his guild stipend and his right to enter licensed

29
00:01:30.045 --> 00:01:33.160
gate facilities.

30
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.818
Cast out into the neon-drenched alleys of the Lower District,

31
00:01:36.818 --> 00:01:40.476
the cold rain soaked through Ethan’s frayed trench-coat.

32
00:01:40.476 --> 00:01:43.018
Every step felt like wading through lead.

33
00:01:43.018 --> 00:01:46.800
His mana core throbbed with a dull, sickening ache—the familiar

34
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.582
burning sensation of a biological system running on empty.

35
00:01:50.582 --> 00:01:53.744
He was twenty-two, penniless, and marked as dead weight by

36
00:01:53.744 --> 00:01:56.906
the most powerful syndicate in the capital.

37
00:01:57.648 --> 00:02:00.811
In a forgotten service corridor beneath the monorail tracks, Ethan’s

38
00:02:00.811 --> 00:02:03.974
knees finally buckled.

39
00:02:03.974 --> 00:02:05.712
His vital signs cratered.

40
00:02:05.712 --> 00:02:08.910
His vision tunnelled into pitch darkness as his heart rhythm

41
00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.108
stuttered to a near standstill.

42
00:02:12.108 --> 00:02:13.568
Two percent vitality.

43
00:02:13.568 --> 00:02:16.488
The threshold where mortal biology ceases.

44
00:02:16.488 --> 00:02:19.164
Yet, at the absolute edge of clinical death, the ambient

45
00:02:19.164 --> 00:02:21.840
air grew motionless.

46
00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.899
The sound of pouring rain halted in mid-air.

47
00:02:24.899 --> 00:02:28.201
A crimson interface, forged from dark obsidian glass, crystallised directly

48
00:02:28.201 --> 00:02:31.503
before his retinas.

49
00:02:31.503 --> 00:02:36.021
Emergency Protocol Initialised: Host Biological Failure Imminent.

50
00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:38.523
Celestial Core Diagnostics Complete.

51
00:02:38.523 --> 00:02:41.373
Dormant Sovereign Protocol: Synchronised.

52
00:02:41.373 --> 00:02:45.266
Unlike the fragile blue interfaces issued by the International Hunter

53
00:02:45.266 --> 00:02:49.159
Ministry, this system bore no rank limits.

54
00:02:49.159 --> 00:02:50.480
No guild oversight.

55
00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.446
A cascade of warm, liquid fire surged outward from his

56
00:02:53.446 --> 00:02:56.412
fractured spine, burning away the necrotic tissue of his ruined

57
00:02:56.412 --> 00:02:59.378
channels.

58
00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:04.557
His notification log flashed a single baseline calibration: Host Physical

59
00:03:04.557 --> 00:03:09.736
Attributes Re-Indexed: Base Constitution Allocated: Two Hundred Points.

60
00:03:12.096 --> 00:03:13.538
Ethan rose to his feet.

61
00:03:13.538 --> 00:03:15.920
The persistent ache that had plagued his chest for seven

62
00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.302
years had vanished.

63
00:03:18.302 --> 00:03:21.457
In its place was a dense, heavy stillness—a weight distribution

64
00:03:21.457 --> 00:03:24.612
within his muscles that felt less like biological tissue and

65
00:03:24.612 --> 00:03:27.767
more like forged tungsten.

66
00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:31.779
The system displayed a strict requirement: Current Level: 1.

67
00:03:31.779 --> 00:03:35.477
Vessel Saturation: Zero of Five Thousand Experience Points.

68
00:03:35.477 --> 00:03:38.214
To understand what two hundred points in Constitution truly meant,

69
00:03:38.214 --> 00:03:40.951
he needed a proving ground where civilian eyes could not

70
00:03:40.951 --> 00:03:43.688
follow.

71
00:03:43.688 --> 00:03:48.076
Sector Nine harboured an unregistered sewer fissure—a low-tier sub-gate that

72
00:03:48.076 --> 00:03:52.464
the municipal authorities had deemed too unprofitable to purge.

73
00:03:52.464 --> 00:03:55.285
Dropping through the rusted maintenance hatch, Ethan landed in the

74
00:03:55.285 --> 00:03:58.106
subterranean catacombs.

75
00:03:58.106 --> 00:04:00.801
The air reeked of damp sulphur and old rot.

76
00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:03.434
In the shadows ahead, three pairs of venomous crimson eyes

77
00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:06.067
